  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find the mean number of vegetarian customers for each day:\n\n$$\n\\overset{¯}{x}=\\frac{145}{7}=20.71\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places.\n\nThe $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set. Rewriting this in terms of $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{z}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard deviation $\\sigma $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\frac{x-\\overset{¯}{x}}{z} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-20.71}{-1.5} \\\\  & =3.81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nto $2$ decimal places.",
